      "tail": "```text\nVERDICT: CLEAN\n\nBOUNDARY: The valuation is defined only for nonzero series; zero is excluded from every\nclause that mentions v or lc. The product's leading index p+q is exactly the sum of the\nvaluations, and the only contributing term is (p,q) because any other pair would involve\nan index below the support lower bound. The sum cases are partitioned into\nv(f)<v(g) (the lower valuation dominates), v(f)=v(g) with non-cancelling leading\ncoefficients, and the residual case where cancellation may occur; the general lower\nbound v(f+g) ≥ min{v(f),v(g)} is proved directly from support lower bounds. The\nnegative case preserves valuation because negation is pointwise. No choice,\nlimiting argument, or hidden division is used. The integers are totally ordered,\nso min is well-defined. The proof correctly separates strict inequalities and\nendpoint indices, and the possibility f+g=0 is explicitly noted as excluded in\nclause 5. All boundary cases (empty support, degenerate cancellation, off-by-one\nin the product convolution) are either inapplicable or explicitly checked.\n\nSOURCES: Every cited item used by the target was inspected in its full supplied\ntext: def-formal-laurent-series, lem-laurent-series-ring, def-field,\nthm-reals-ordered-field, thm-int-ordered-ring, def-int-order. L1 matches the\nvaluation definition; L2 matches the ring lemma (finiteness, vanishing below m+n)\nand the operation definitions; L3 matches the field axioms for ℝ; L4 matches the\ntotal order and additive compatibility for ℤ. Each use in the proof is directly\nsupported by the quoted source.\n\nCHECKED: The title, the public claim (Statement clauses 1–5), every numbered\nproof step (1.1–3.1), and the absence of Remarks were read and verified.\n```"
    },
    {
      "id": "thm-laurent-series-field",
      "tail": "```text\nVERDICT: CLEAN\nBOUNDARY: All required boundary cases are correctly treated. The zero element is not inverted, and the construction for nonzero f handles the degenerate case u=0 (where g=1_K) and the identity case f=1_K. The index splits at k<0, k=0, k≥1 are exhaustive and each branch is verified. The powers uⁿ are supplied uniquely by recursion, and every coefficient sum is an explicit finite sum. No counterexample exists; the explicit inverse formula is valid for every nonzero f ∈ K.\nSOURCES: Every supplied cited item (def-formal-laurent-series, lem-laurent-series-ring, lem-laurent-valuation, def-field, thm-reals-ordered-field, thm-recursion, thm-induction-principle, def-natural-numbers) was inspected. The quoted passages in the proof contract match the source texts, and each citation licenses the exact use made in the proof.\nCHECKED: The title, the public statement, every numbered proof step (1.1 through 9.1), the Scratch, and both Remarks were read and verified. No mathematical defect, over-assertion, or invalid inference was found.\n```"
    },
    {
      "id": "thm-laurent-ordered-field",
      "tail": "VERDICT: CLEAN\nBOUNDARY: Zero element is explicitly separated in step 1.1 and the base case of step 2.3. The one/identity element is verified in steps 1.3 and 2.3. Degenerate equal‑valuation addition that would cancel cannot occur because $f,g\\in P$ forces $\\operatorname{lc}(f)+\\operatorname{lc}(g)>0$, so clause 4 of L3 applies and the sum remains in $P$. The empty carrier is not applicable. The endpoint $\\operatorname{lc}(f)=0$ is excluded for nonzero $f$ by definition; no hidden extended‑real convention or non‑constructive choice is used. The statement is not a biconditional. Attempted construction of a counterexample to the positive‑cone axioms failed: the order defined by $P$ satisfies trichotomy, closure under addition and multiplication, and yields a total order compatible with the field operations.\nSOURCES: All supplied source texts for L1–L9 (def‑formal‑laurent‑series, lem‑laurent‑series‑ring, lem‑laurent‑valuation, thm‑laurent‑series‑field, def‑ordered‑field, def‑archimedean‑field, def‑abs‑value, thm‑reals‑ordered‑field, thm‑induction‑principle, def‑natural‑numbers, thm‑int‑ordered‑ring) were inspected in full. Every fact stated in the target exactly reflects the source’s statement, and each proof‑step use respects the source’s hypotheses, quantifiers, and conclusions.\nCHECKED: The title, the public statement (clauses 1‑3), every numbered proof step 1.1‑5.1, and the Remarks section were read and found mathematically accurate and logically consistent."
