 - **Blocking gates:** read-only enforcement passes. The generated-risk receipt fails on the eight refuter-dependent Wave 6 dispositions; `risk-report --require-reviewed` fails on the 93 high/critical records; independent repair certification is 0/5; and the orchestrator-owned URL-liveness table is still absent. These failures are truthful stage state, not gate waivers.
 - **Exact next action when outbound transport is available without a permission prompt:** rerun the two pilots; dispatch the remaining five Terra certification reads and the 126 prepared DeepSeek tasks at the enforced lane caps; adjudicate every finding against disk; repair only confirmed defects and independently recertify any Alpha-authored repair; then complete genrisk and risk-review dispositions, finish the semantic edge ledger, merge contracts, and run the full A6 gates. The orchestrator may run A7 only after that handoff.
 - **A8 status:** not active. The run state has no A7 result and a judge budget of zero, so there are no Wave 6 judge rejections to adjudicate and no `pre-a8` stage snapshot. The exact A8 edited-item/rejudge list is therefore empty.
+
+## Recovery continuation — A6 independent reads available (2026-08-08)
+
+- **Baseline and current text reverified before resuming:** `HEAD`, `main`, and `origin/main` are all `84c52d136b16758747e7283118420cf88009148d`; the inherited dirty/untracked workspace remains intact. All 126 current refuter task hashes match the normalized text now on disk, the sorted `id<TAB>normalized-item-sha256` aggregate remains `1f81470195394f158c9fde2470b2a55b7765fb144b63342785ea104814dffe94`, and the five repair-certifier task hashes still equal the five hashes recorded in the preceding recovery receipt.
+- **Required recovery surface read:** `CLAUDE.md`, `AUDIT-WORKFLOW.md`, `README.md`, `SCHEMA.md`, `QUALITY-CONTROLS.md`, `briefs/audit-alpha.md`, `research/audit/RESUME.md`, this full report, `wave6-A0.md`, `wave6-A3-alpha-concurrence-task.md`, `wave6-A3.md`, all three findings files, all three provenance ledgers, all three page manifests, `wave6-split.json`, `wave6-batch-split.json`, `wave6-audit-manifest.json`, all three namespaced contracts and the merged contract, `wave6-touches.json`, `wave6-impact-template.json`, `wave6-impact.json`, `wave6-url-liveness.json`, `genrisk.json`, `wave6-run-state.json`, all 126 assembled refuter tasks, all five certifier tasks, and all 131 corresponding result records were read or exhaustively parsed. The relevant five material items, eleven generated seeds, failed-URL consumers, and generated-risk consumers were checked from current disk.
+- **The earlier transport blocker is superseded by disk evidence:** all 126 tool-less DeepSeek V4 Pro audit-refuter calls subsequently completed read-only with exit zero and `VERDICT: CLEAN`; all five GPT 5.6 Terra certifiers completed read-only with exit zero and `VERDICT: CERTIFIED`. Their result models, sandboxes, target labels, and current task hashes were verified. No returned finding alleges a fatal defect.
+- **Inherited classifications and receipts reverified:** all 11 D2 rows still carry `alpha_concurred: true`; strict proof-contract validation remains 106/106 with no errors or warnings; the manifest still contains 1,390 accounted edges; the current split remains 121 pure / 5 material; and the generated-risk receipt still has exactly eight Wave 6 load-bearing seeds awaiting Alpha disposition. The touch ledger has the inherited `pre-A4`/`post-A4` stage snapshots and five inherited per-item snapshots; Alpha will take no A6 snapshot.
+- **URL prerequisite delivered:** `wave6-url-liveness.json` covers all 92 scoped URLs (89 live, three unsuccessful checks). The Padua PDF failure is a timeout against a still-current official resource and will be retained. The dead MIT copy is redundant with the live UCR source already cited on the same six items and will be removed. The dead legacy UCL host has an exact live official `www.homepages.ucl.ac.uk` replacement; Alpha will update the two affected items and their provenance rows, then obtain independent final-text certification for every Alpha-authored source repair.
+- **Inherited open actions:** disposition the eight load-bearing Wave 6 generated seeds; add complete high/critical risk reviews from the current DeepSeek readings; record the five certified Beta repairs and the Alpha source corrections in the repair receipt; write the five owner-delegated `verification.verified` stamps only against certified final text; regenerate and verify the current impact receipt; merge contracts; and run all A6 quality gates. A8 remains inactive because A7 has not run and the judge budget is zero.
+- **Exact next action:** make only the eight URL-source metadata corrections described above, update the two matching topology provenance records, assemble final-text Terra certification tasks for those Alpha-authored repairs, and dispatch them read-only before stamping or closing any A6 receipt.
